<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Njinga of Ndongo and Matamba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1583–1663</span> · Also known as Njinga Mbande, Queen Nzinga, Ana de Sousa Nzinga Mbande</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Njinga Mbande was queen of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbundu">Mbundu</a> kingdoms of Ndongo and Matamba in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>. She negotiated with the Portuguese in 1622, became ruler of Ndongo in 1624 and, driven out, conquered Matamba around 1631. She allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> against Portugal in the 1640s and resisted Portuguese expansion for decades, making peace in 1656.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/njinga-of-ndongo-and-matamba.jpg" alt="Njinga of Ndongo and Matamba" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Achille Devéria · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ann_Zingha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
